                 "difficult", "hard to work with", "interrupting", "interrupts", "talks over",
                 "takes credit", "credit for my work", "undermines", "undermining",
                 "annoying", "annoyed", "hate", "hates", "toxic", "bully", "bullied",
                 "bullying", "not invited", "left out", "leaves me out", "mean to me",
                 "clique", "two faced", "gossip", "gossiping", "falling out", "fell out",
                 "argument", "row with",
                 # a friend gone silent is friends.py's friend-quiet, not how to meet people:
                 # this row was answering "my friend isn t talking to me" with the running club
                 "isn t talking to me", "isnt talking to me", "not talking to me",
                 "wont talk to me", "won t talk to me", "stopped talking to me",
                 "isn t speaking to me", "isnt speaking to me", "not speaking to me",
                 "wont speak to me", "won t speak to me", "stopped speaking to me",
                 "havent heard from", "haven t heard from", "not heard from", "no word from",
                 "gone silent", "blanked me", "blocked me", "has blocked me", "avoiding me",
                 "off with me",
                 # A friend who is being unkind is the hurt-my-feelings row, not a person
                 # looking for where to meet anyone: "my friend is being mean to me" and
